# ============================================================
# PAL EMITTER
# BUILD: v60u_mars_exact_inplace_state_write_terminator_v1
# Paired executable/readable rendering + authoritative ABI custody
# ============================================================
#
# Consumes:
#   func.exec_root / func.exec_tree
#   func.formula_nodes / func.var_nodes
#   func.phi_nodes
#   func.var_map
#   func.condition_vars
#   func.return_vars
#
# PHI/drop-in metadata from PALPHIfolder_presentation_dropins_v2:
#   func.phi_dropins
#   func.phi_dropins_by_pred
#   func.phi_dropins_by_join
#
# Presentation metadata:
#   func.inline_only_sids
#   func.suppress_assign_sids
#   func.materialize_sids
#   func.local_target_sids
#   func.preferred_expr_by_sid
#   func.phi_source_foldable_sids
#
# Design:
#   - CALL/CALLIND are never inlined during normal expression rendering.
#   - Materialized CALL outputs are emitted as statements.
#   - Suppressed SSA bridge assignments are hidden only if their semantic
#     replacement is emitted through PHI drop-ins or expression rendering.
#   - PHI drop-ins close transitions:
#         v_796 = local_1c + v_2808
#         local_1c = local_1c + v_2808
#   - Local initializers are never suppressed.
#   - INDIRECT is a metadata-only storage-version transition.  It is never
#     rendered as Python syntax and never treated as COPY.
#   - Readable mode names the HighVariable storage family.  Executable mode
#     reads/writes address-tied families through PAL's existing memory helpers.
#   - ABI-D entry/call/return plans and ABI-F convergence contracts are
#     consumed verbatim.  The emitter never recovers carrier placement from
#     parameter names, expressions, or target spelling.
#   - The executable projection uses one explicit ``abi_context`` boundary.
#     ``c_abi_get``, ``c_abi_call``, and ``c_abi_return`` are PALABI transport
#     primitives; their arguments come only from the published custody
#     contracts.  Numeric helpers remain isolated in PALhelpers.
#   - ExecDispatch / ExecCase are rendered from SGL's semantic multiway tree.
#     Selector expressions pass through the same ABI, compute, storage-custody,
#     and identity gates as ordinary expressions. Case-edge PHI transitions are
#     emitted only at their exact predecessor block inside the owning ExecCase.
#   - A raw terminal JMP whose exact destination matches one ABI-planned CALL
#     is a tail transfer, not CALL + synthetic local RETURN.  The emitter
#     forwards the c_abi_call result directly and never manufactures return 0.
#   - SemanticGraph v35 / SGL v66 / PHIfolder v29 temporal-snapshot custody
#     is consumed by exact SID. Historical COPY epochs and values derived from
#     historical/later epochs are never folded into the live state family.
#     The emitter refuses publication if the exact snapshot assignment or
#     independent derived assignment disappears, aliases back to state, or
#     collapses an order-sensitive operation into x op x.
#   - A v50 direct-join transition between distinct SIDs cannot become an
#     identity no-op merely because a revoked PHI source alias left both names
#     projected alike. Exact PHIfolder v30/v33 receipts reopen only that one
#     predecessor-local assignment gate; unrelated var_map entries are never
#     rewritten by the emitter.
#   - PALemitter v60 activates exact loop_exit_edge placements only in the
#     post-loop-body/pre-join phase. The frozen transition edge and owner
#     occurrence come from PHIfolder/PALSGL authority; sibling exits are never
#     activated by proximity.
#   - v60d closes only an exact pending PHIfolder v43d typed direct-join
#     loop-exit ticket at the guaranteed post-loop/pre-join boundary. A writer
#     attempt becomes scheduler-emitted only after an accepted terminal receipt.
#   - Exact PHIfolder v44 source-binding receipts and existing ABI-D/F exact
#     SID bindings are consumed before a raw PHI source name. The emitter never
#     derives a replacement name from spelling, ordinal position, or CFG order.
#   - PHIfolder v40's phi_execution_plan_v2 is consumed before source/dynamic/
#     selector aliases, textual identity, or canonical-owner absorption. One
#     semantic transition may authorize several frozen ExecTree placements.
#     Terminal receipts are keyed by (transition_id, placement_id); rejected
#     probes remain non-terminal evidence. The emitter never reconstructs a
#     transition, placement, owner, or RHS while this contract is active.
#   - v60f records exact branch-closure definition-fusion receipts. When the
#     defining op of a PHI source was already emitted directly into the exact
#     target on the exact predecessor edge, the later plan ticket is satisfied
#     without emitting a stale ``target = v_N`` copy. No textual alias or
#     target-name heuristic can authorize this suppression.
#   - v60g merges that exact definition-fusion terminal disposition into the
#     historical v50 direct-join satisfaction ledger. The v50 audit accepts
#     fusion only after independently verifying the canonical transition,
#     exact edge, proven fusion receipt, accepted execution-plan receipt, and
#     preserved defining line. It never converts fusion into a rendered PHI
#     assignment and never weakens ordinary direct-join cardinality.
#   - v60h records the same protocol receipt when an ordinary op assignment,
#     rather than the branch-closure path, is committed under source-SID
#     custody directly into the exact PHI target execution name. Admission is
#     edge-, SID-, occurrence-, line-, and write-order exact; raw ``v_*``
#     spelling never authorizes suppression.
#   - v60i consumes PHIfolder's exact selector-passthrough records. A used
#     value-selector PHI whose transparent incoming source was intentionally
#     suppressed must receive the concrete transparent-chain leaf (for example
#     ``v_selector = local_state``), never the now-unmaterialized bridge SID.
#     The selector assignment remains executable; only the ghost bridge spelling
#     is replaced after exact transition, edge, SID, opcode-chain and leaf-name
#     agreement.
#   - v60j closes the protected-bridge seam for required multi-arm selector
#     convergence inside a loop. A generic protected COPY temp remains guarded,
#     but an exact PHIfolder selector-passthrough arm may consume its concrete
#     leaf when the frozen placement ticket, source materialization proof,
#     source-definition receipt, non-temporal flags, predecessor edge and
#     terminal consumer obligation all agree. The published placement remains a
#     predecessor-edge ticket; the emitter does not relabel it as a loop exit.
#   - v60l closes the adjacent carryover seam after a native source definition
#     was already materialized into its exact PHI execution owner before the
#     control flow fans out to one or several authorized predecessor tickets.
#     Each placement receives its own proof ticket from the same dominating
#     assignment commit. COPY/CAST bridges, selector arms, temporal snapshots,
#     inferred names and displaced owner values remain outside this profile.
#   - v60n admits the same dominating-owner receipt on an exact loop_exit_edge
#     only when the prebuilt v60 loop-edge scheduler publishes one matching
#     transition/placement/edge/terminal key with proven source materialization.
#     This closes branch-adjacent loop-header carryovers without treating every
#     loop-exit-shaped occurrence as a generic predecessor or weakening v60.
#   - v60p adds a fail-closed execution-alias epoch ticket after v60l. When
#     the exact source SID is already projected through the exact PHI target
#     name, one live native assignment in the authoritative defining block may
#     satisfy each authorized placement. Only a later write in that same
#     defining occurrence displaces it; ancestor/sibling writes do not.
#   - v60r closes repeated-source multi-backedge fan-out. When two canonical
#     PHI transitions into the same join carry the same immutable SSA source
#     into the same target, the complete v56 plan inventory may satisfy each
#     placement from one concrete owner definition only when both placement
#     proofs cite the exact same accepted definition receipt and exactly one
#     live owner assignment exists in that defining occurrence. Traversal order,
#     raw SSA spelling and prior peer consumption are not authority.
# ============================================================


